From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicholas Gigliotti <ndgigliotti@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 12:28:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: correct Linux rwsem conditional acquisition status

down_read_trylock() and down_write_trylock() return 1 when they acquire
the lock and 0 when they cannot, unlike down_trylock(), which returns 0
on success. os_cond_acquire_rwlock_read() and
os_cond_acquire_rwlock_write() checked the result as if it were
down_trylock(): a successful acquire was reported as
NV_ERR_TIMEOUT_RETRY with the lock left held, and a failed one was
reported as NV_OK without the lock.

The only RM user is the API_LOCK_FLAGS_COND_ACQUIRE branch of
rmapiLockAcquire(), and no caller in this tree passes that flag, so this
is currently dead code. Fix it so a future conditional API lock acquire
doesn't leak the lock (deadlock) or run without it.

References:
- NVIDIA/open-gpu-kernel-modules PR 1424
---
 kernel-open/nvidia/os-interface.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia/os-interface.c b/kernel-open/nvidia/os-interface.c
index b4369be8..e7d9607f 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia/os-interface.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia/os-interface.c
@@ -345,7 +345,7 @@ NV_STATUS NV_API_CALL os_cond_acquire_rwlock_read(void *pRwLock)
 {
     os_rwlock_t *os_rwlock = (os_rwlock_t *)pRwLock;
 
-    if (down_read_trylock(&os_rwlock->sem))
+    if (!down_read_trylock(&os_rwlock->sem))
     {
         return NV_ERR_TIMEOUT_RETRY;
     }
@@ -357,7 +357,7 @@ NV_STATUS NV_API_CALL os_cond_acquire_rwlock_write(void *pRwLock)
 {
     os_rwlock_t *os_rwlock = (os_rwlock_t *)pRwLock;
 
-    if (down_write_trylock(&os_rwlock->sem))
+    if (!down_write_trylock(&os_rwlock->sem))
     {
         return NV_ERR_TIMEOUT_RETRY;
     }
